"Welcome to the Riverside Museum. The main entrance is on King Street, opposite the public library. The museum opens at nine thirty and closes at five, except on Thursdays when it remains open until eight. Admission to the permanent collection is free, but the special exhibition costs six dollars for adults. Children under sixteen enter the exhibition free. Bags larger than a small backpack must be left in the lockers beside the information desk. The café is on the ground floor next to the garden entrance. The education room is upstairs, directly above the café. Guided tours begin at eleven and two. Today, the eleven o'clock tour is cancelled because the guide is ill, so the first tour will be at two. Photography is allowed in most galleries, but flash is prohibited. The quietest time to visit is usually between three and four on weekday afternoons.": "audio/eb9f6bf3c620.mp3",
"So, how is the group project on student transport progressing?": "audio/4c4327d12804.mp3",
"We finished the online survey. We expected about a hundred responses, but we received one hundred and forty-two.": "audio/4859c7236778.mp3",
"The problem is that most responses came from first-year students.": "audio/7e29c9bb621c.mp3",
"Then you should mention that limitation in the report.": "audio/b8e29406d36e.mp3",
"We also planned to interview bus drivers, but the transport company has not replied.": "audio/ff35402d546a.mp3",
"Instead, we interviewed twelve students who cycle to campus.": "audio/40ce1179c397.mp3",
"Good. What did you learn?": "audio/fbd5ba371fa2.mp3",
"Cost was important, but reliability mattered more.": "audio/6edcee78c8cf.mp3",
"And safety was the main concern for cyclists, especially after dark.": "audio/4cd844463574.mp3",
"What about your presentation?": "audio/27b19207e091.mp3",
"I can explain the survey results.": "audio/cbab22586440.mp3",
"I'll cover the interviews.": "audio/3ed155dc6d89.mp3",
