"No. Choose two charts that best support your conclusions. Put the extra data in an appendix.": "audio/4381ef993994.mp3",
"Today we'll examine how urban tree canopies influence heat in cities. Dense building materials such as concrete and asphalt absorb solar energy during the day and release it slowly at night. This contributes to what is known as the urban heat island effect. Trees can reduce local temperatures in two main ways: by providing shade and through evapotranspiration, a process in which water moves from leaves into the atmosphere. However, simply planting more trees does not guarantee equal cooling everywhere. The size of the canopy, the species selected, soil volume and water availability all matter. Recent studies suggest that neighbourhoods with very low canopy cover may experience the greatest benefit from new planting. Yet maintenance is crucial. Young trees need regular watering, and poorly selected species may damage pavements or struggle in dry conditions. Planners also need to consider equity. In many cities, wealthier districts have more mature trees than lower-income areas. Therefore, urban forestry programmes increasingly prioritise neighbourhoods with high heat exposure and limited existing canopy. The aim is not only to plant trees, but to create a healthy, long-term urban forest.": "audio/6d69a1f9d145.mp3",
"We are expecting sixteen participants. I should clarify that: not sixty, but one six, sixteen. My surname is Mason, M A S O N. The session was originally planned for nine o'clock, but it will now begin at nine thirty.": "audio/0e0ac9b3d59a.mp3",
"The workshop will be held on Thursday, not Tuesday as stated in the earlier email. Please go to room twenty-seven. If you have questions, contact Ms Parker. That's Parker, P A R K E R.": "audio/d5e55efb5d28.mp3",
"The training session is on Friday the twenty-first of November. Registration opens at eight forty-five, and the talk begins at nine fifteen. Participants should bring a laptop. Lunch is provided in the main hall.": "audio/538de65ea52a.mp3",
"Enter through the main gate. The reception desk is immediately on your left. Walk straight ahead to the stairs, then turn right. The seminar room is opposite the café and next to the lift.": "audio/e32349f3b8e5.mp3",
"We first considered holding the event in March, but that was too early. April was possible, although several speakers were unavailable, so the final date is the twelfth of May.": "audio/ad81e3bbff70.mp3",
"Anna prefers online training because it saves travel time. Bilal likes face-to-face sessions because discussion feels easier. Carla prefers a blended format that combines both approaches.": "audio/34395ea908a9.mp3",
