"Today we will examine sleep and memory. First, research suggests that sleep helps stabilise newly learned information. Second, deep sleep appears particularly important for some forms of memory. However, researchers caution that sleep quality, timing and individual differences all influence the effect.": "audio/3b159b324676.mp3",
